1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,922
I want to tell you about six minutes. The most
important six minutes in Sarah's career.

2
00:00:03,922 --> 00:00:07,844
She walked into a meeting room earning fifty-eight thousand.
She walked out earning a hundred and twenty.

3
00:00:07,844 --> 00:00:11,766
It was not luck. It was not a clever
trick taught in a book.

4
00:00:11,766 --> 00:00:15,688
It was three small choices she made
in those six minutes.

5
00:00:15,688 --> 00:00:19,610
Most professionals get this moment wrong. Here is
exactly what she did, and why it worked.

6
00:00:19,610 --> 00:00:23,533
She has been at her company for three
years and eight months.

7
00:00:23,533 --> 00:00:27,455
She knows exactly what she is worth. She
has done the research.

8
00:00:27,455 --> 00:00:31,377
Two competitor offers sit in her drawer.
She has not used them.

9
00:00:31,377 --> 00:00:35,299
Today is her annual review. The conversation
she has avoided for a year.

10
00:00:35,299 --> 00:00:39,221
Her boss is a kind man. That is
part of the problem.

11
00:00:39,221 --> 00:00:43,143
Kind bosses give kind raises. Three
percent. Maybe four.

12
00:00:43,143 --> 00:00:47,065
She has watched colleagues leave for
forty-thousand-pound jumps.

13
00:00:47,065 --> 00:00:50,987
She has stayed because she likes the team. The work.
The familiar walk to the kitchen.

14
00:00:50,987 --> 00:00:54,909
But she has been paying for that
loyalty every single month.

15
00:00:54,909 --> 00:00:58,831
Today she is going to ask for
what she is worth.

16
00:00:58,831 --> 00:01:02,754
She wakes at six. She prepares like she is
interviewing for the job she already has.

17
00:01:02,754 --> 00:01:06,676
She makes a list. Three columns. Achievements.
Comparables. Counter-arguments.

18
00:01:06,676 --> 00:01:10,598
She practises one sentence in the mirror
until it sounds natural.

19
00:01:10,598 --> 00:01:14,520
The sentence is: I need a hundred and
twenty for me to stay.

20
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:18,442
She does not soften it. She does not pad it.
She does not apologise for it.

21
00:01:18,442 --> 00:01:22,364
She does not dread this conversation.
She is going to lead it.

22
00:01:22,364 --> 00:01:26,286
At nine she walks into the office. Coffee
in hand. Completely normal.

23
00:01:26,286 --> 00:01:30,208
At ten the calendar reminder fires. Review
with Mark, eleven thirty.

24
00:01:30,208 --> 00:01:34,130
At eleven she stops working. She rereads her
list. She closes her notebook.

25
00:01:34,130 --> 00:01:38,052
At eleven twenty-eight she walks across the
office to the glass meeting room.

26
00:01:38,052 --> 00:01:41,975
Mark is already there. Laptop open.
Friendly smile. He likes her.

27
00:01:41,975 --> 00:01:45,897
He starts the way kind bosses start. He
asks how her year has been.

28
00:01:45,897 --> 00:01:49,819
She tells him. Briefly. She does not list. She
tells him she had a good year.

29
00:01:49,819 --> 00:01:53,741
He nods. He brings up her file
on his screen.

30
00:01:53,741 --> 00:01:57,663
He says the team values her. He says she
has grown significantly.

31
00:01:57,663 --> 00:02:01,585
He pauses. Like he is about to
give her a gift.

32
00:02:01,585 --> 00:02:05,507
He says they would like to offer her a
four percent raise.

33
00:02:05,507 --> 00:02:09,429
Four percent on fifty-eight is two thousand three
hundred and twenty pounds a year.

34
00:02:09,429 --> 00:02:13,351
After tax, fewer than fifteen hundred. About a
hundred and twenty pounds a month.

35
00:02:13,351 --> 00:02:17,273
She does not react. She does not nod.
She does not thank him.

36
00:02:17,273 --> 00:02:21,196
She lets the number sit between them.
Five seconds. Then ten.

37
00:02:21,196 --> 00:02:25,118
Mark fills the silence. He says he
knows it is not a lot.

38
00:02:25,118 --> 00:02:29,040
He says budgets are tight this year. He says
he hopes she understands.

39
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:32,962
Now is the moment she has practised.
She does not rush it.

40
00:02:32,962 --> 00:02:36,884
She says, Mark, I appreciate the offer. I
want to be honest with you.

41
00:02:36,884 --> 00:02:40,806
She says, I have done some research. And I
have had two conversations.

42
00:02:40,806 --> 00:02:44,728
She does not name the companies. She
does not show the offers.

43
00:02:44,728 --> 00:02:48,650
She says, The market for someone with my work is between one
hundred and ten and one hundred and thirty.

44
00:02:48,650 --> 00:02:52,572
She says, I love the team. I would
prefer to stay.

45
00:02:52,572 --> 00:02:56,494
She says, I need a hundred and
twenty for me to stay.

46
00:02:56,494 --> 00:03:00,417
Then she stops. She does not explain. She does not
justify. She does not add anything.

47
00:03:00,417 --> 00:03:04,339
Mark looks at her. He looks at his
laptop. He looks at her again.

48
00:03:04,339 --> 00:03:08,261
He says he was not expecting this. She
does not fill the silence.

49
00:03:08,261 --> 00:03:12,183
He says he will need to talk to his
director. She nods, once.

50
00:03:12,183 --> 00:03:16,105
She says, I understand. Take
whatever time you need.

51
00:03:16,105 --> 00:03:20,027
She says, I would like the offer in writing
before I respond either way.

52
00:03:20,027 --> 00:03:23,949
She stands up. She thanks him for his
time. She walks out.

53
00:03:23,949 --> 00:03:27,871
Six minutes have passed. The meeting ended
seventeen minutes early.

54
00:03:27,871 --> 00:03:31,793
Mark sits alone for two of those minutes
before he calls his director.

55
00:03:31,793 --> 00:03:35,715
By the end of the day she has an email. The
number is one hundred and fifteen.

56
00:03:35,715 --> 00:03:39,638
She does not reply that evening. She does
not reply the next morning.

57
00:03:39,638 --> 00:03:43,560
She replies at three the next
afternoon. One paragraph. Calm.

58
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:47,482
She thanks him for moving so quickly. She says
one hundred and fifteen is close.

59
00:03:47,482 --> 00:03:51,404
She says she would accept one hundred and twenty
plus an additional week of leave.

60
00:03:51,404 --> 00:03:55,326
She signs off. Closes her laptop. Does
not refresh her inbox.

61
00:03:55,326 --> 00:03:59,248
The reply comes back at five. One hundred and
twenty. The extra leave approved.

62
00:03:59,248 --> 00:04:03,170
She accepts in writing. One short professional sentence.
Thank you. I look forward to continuing.

63
00:04:03,170 --> 00:04:07,092
She closes the laptop. She does not
tell anyone for two days.

64
00:04:07,092 --> 00:04:11,014
Her base salary has more than doubled in nine
minutes of actual conversation.

65
00:04:11,014 --> 00:04:14,936
After tax that is approximately three thousand
four hundred pounds a month more.

66
00:04:14,936 --> 00:04:18,859
Forty thousand more a year. For the rest
of her career. Compounded.

67
00:04:18,859 --> 00:04:22,781
She did not threaten. She did not show
her competing offers.

68
00:04:22,781 --> 00:04:26,703
She did not list her achievements. She did
not ask for permission.

69
00:04:26,703 --> 00:04:30,625
She named her number. She held the
silence. She left.

70
00:04:30,625 --> 00:04:34,547
That is the whole technique. Three
things. Six minutes.

71
00:04:34,547 --> 00:04:38,469
Most professionals do not ask. They
wait to be given.

72
00:04:38,469 --> 00:04:42,391
They confuse loyalty with patience. They
confuse politeness with weakness.

73
00:04:42,391 --> 00:04:46,313
They believe a good boss will
eventually notice their worth.

74
00:04:46,313 --> 00:04:50,235
Good bosses notice. They still pay
you the budget number.

75
00:04:50,235 --> 00:04:54,157
Sarah's boss did not become unkind
when she asked for more.

76
00:04:54,157 --> 00:04:58,080
He paid her more because she asked for
more. He still liked her.

77
00:04:58,080 --> 00:05:02,002
The conversation was not a fight. It
was a clarification.

78
00:05:02,002 --> 00:05:05,924
She told him what she was
worth. He paid it.

79
00:05:05,924 --> 00:05:09,846
Three things she did. She named her
number, specifically.

80
00:05:09,846 --> 00:05:13,768
She held the silence. She did not
justify or explain.

81
00:05:13,768 --> 00:05:17,690
She did not respond immediately. She
gave herself time.

82
00:05:17,690 --> 00:05:21,612
That is six minutes. That is forty
thousand pounds a year.

83
00:05:21,612 --> 00:05:25,534
Compounded across a career, that single
conversation is worth more than a house.

84
00:05:25,534 --> 00:05:29,456
Have the conversation. Most of you
have earned it already.
